The graph of $y = 4\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi x}{4}\right)$ and the line $y = 2\sqrt{2}$ are shown for $0 \le x \le 16$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.8, xmax=18.5, ymin=-5, ymax=5,
  xtick={4, 8, 12, 16},
  ytick={-4, 4},
  samples=200, clip=false,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=12cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0:16] {4*sin(deg(pi*x/4))};
\addplot[thick, red, domain=0:16] {2.82843};
\node[red, anchor=west] at (axis cs:16.3,2.82843) {$y=2\sqrt{2}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The curve has period $8$, and $x=1$ is one solution of $4\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi x}{4}\right) = 2\sqrt{2}$. Find all solutions in $0 \le x \le 16$.

The graph of $y = 3\tan\left(\dfrac{x}{2}\right)$ and the line $y = 3$ are shown for $0 \le x \le 4\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.6, xmax=13.6, ymin=-9.5, ymax=9.5,
  xtick={3.1416, 6.2832, 9.4248, 12.5664},
  xticklabels={$\pi$, $2\pi$, $3\pi$, $4\pi$},
  ytick={-6, 3, 6},
  samples=100, clip=false,
  restrict y to domain=-9.5:9.5, unbounded coords=jump,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=12cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0:2.4980] {3*tan(deg(x/2))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=3.7852:8.7812] {3*tan(deg(x/2))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=10.0684:12.5664] {3*tan(deg(x/2))};
\addplot[thick, red, domain=0:12.5664] {3};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How many solutions does $3\tan\left(\dfrac{x}{2}\right) = 3$ have for $0 \le x \le 4\pi$? List them.
